//Black ascot bow with a chrysanthemum brooch
# Bow loop in local coordinates: s 0..1 from the knot outward, w around; length le, half-height he,
# half-thickness te. The loop is pinched at the knot and rounded at the end.
bla(s,le)=le*s
blh(s,w,he)=he*sin(pi*s)^0.55*(0.35+0.65*s)*cos(w)
blt(s,w,te)=te*sin(pi*s)^0.5*sin(w)
