//Hair
# Her hair flows from the crown. A lock is described by t, from the crown (0) down to the end of
# the longest hair (1): up to t = 0.15909 it lies on a dome around the head (ha is the angle from the
# crown), below that it falls. hzz(t) is the height, hrx(t) and hry(t) are the half-axes of the ellipse the
# hair lies on at that height: they follow the dome, then keep clear of the shoulders, capelet, arms, book
# and skirt and flare out toward the ends (fitted by the generator). hu(t) is 0 on the dome and grows to 1
# down the fall. hdw keeps a lock's width steady as the hair spreads.
ha(t)=1.5708*min(1,t/0.15909)
hu(t)=max(0,t-0.15909)/0.84091
hzz(t)=12.15+0.825*cos(ha(t))-8.14591*max(0,t-0.15909)
hrx(t)=0.725*sin(ha(t))+34.47883*max(0,t-0.15909)^2+(-78.78553)*max(0,t-0.18909)^2+58.9796*max(0,t-0.21909)^2+(-23.07387)*max(0,t-0.24909)^2+11.66444*max(0,t-0.27409)^2+(-2.95846)*max(0,t-0.29909)^2+(-10.01795)*max(0,t-0.32409)^2+282.68112*max(0,t-0.34909)^2+(-394.01894)*max(0,t-0.37409)^2+176.48215*max(0,t-0.39909)^2+(-183.16716)*max(0,t-0.42909)^2+183.2702*max(0,t-0.46909)^2+(-113.39974)*max(0,t-0.51909)^2+110.55821*max(0,t-0.58909)^2+(-85.74703)*max(0,t-0.67909)^2+36.7042*max(0,t-0.77909)^2+(-12.29261)*max(0,t-0.87909)^2
hry(t)=0.815*sin(ha(t))+34.48179*max(0,t-0.15909)^2+(-78.80637)*max(0,t-0.18909)^2+59.05858*max(0,t-0.21909)^2+(-23.34432)*max(0,t-0.24909)^2+12.40763*max(0,t-0.27409)^2+(-4.99017)*max(0,t-0.29909)^2+0.54628*max(0,t-0.32409)^2+6.06578*max(0,t-0.34909)^2+16.67254*max(0,t-0.37409)^2+(-17.89256)*max(0,t-0.39909)^2+(-8.00727)*max(0,t-0.42909)^2+17.45868*max(0,t-0.46909)^2+(-41.99399)*max(0,t-0.51909)^2+51.12941*max(0,t-0.58909)^2+(-32.14554)*max(0,t-0.67909)^2+15.72228*max(0,t-0.77909)^2+(-11.56127)*max(0,t-0.87909)^2
hdw(t)=min(1,1.54/(hrx(t)+hry(t)))
# Her head is tilted and turned (see the generator); a lock turns with it where it lies on the head and
# hangs straight below. hb(t) is 1 on the head and eases to 0 by t = 0.24909; hs and hk are the sine and
# one minus the cosine of the head's turn times hb.
hb(t)=1-min(1,max(0,(t-0.15909)/0.09))^2*(3-2*min(1,max(0,(t-0.15909)/0.09)))
hs(t)=sin(0.2457*hb(t))
hk(t)=1-cos(0.2457*hb(t))
# A lock is a tube around its own flow line. lpc is the angle of that line around the head: a starting
# angle pb+p0 (0 = straight back, + toward her left) whose part p0 closes up by sg as the hair spreads (sg = 1
# falls straight down, sg = 0 fans out over the shoulders; pb is 0 for the back and pi for the front), a drift dr, and a wave of size am that grows down the
# lock. lrc is how far the line stands off the hair surface: its layer la, and the wave again a quarter turn
# later, so the lock snakes in and out as well as side to side. Across the lock (w runs around it) lwd is
# the half-width and lth the thickness, a crescent lcs with three ridges that is flat underneath. ltp tapers
# the lock toward its end te, and lq runs 0..1 over the last stretch, where the tip turns through three
# quarters of a circle: sideways like a hook, or outward like a scroll.
ltp(t,te)=min(1,max(0,te-t)/0.13)^0.6
lq(t,te)=max(0,1-max(0,te-t)/0.08)
lcs(w)=(0.65*sin(w)+0.35*abs(sin(w)))*(0.78+0.22*cos(2*pi*cos(w)))
lpc(t,pb,p0,sg,dr,am,kk,ph)=pb+p0*(1-sg*(1-hdw(t)))+dr*hu(t)+am*hu(t)^1.5*sin(kk*hu(t)+ph)
lrc(t,la,am,kk,ph)=la*min(1,t/0.04)+0.6*am*hu(t)^1.5*cos(kk*hu(t)+ph)
lwd(t,te,hw)=hw*ltp(t,te)*hdw(t)
lth(t,w,te,th)=th*ltp(t,te)*lcs(w)*min(1,t/0.04)
# A dark cap and an inner sheet under the locks, so no gap shows skin. The cap stops higher above her left
# eye and a little higher above her right eye, where the forehead shows between the bangs as on the sheet.
(0.97*(0.7105*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*cos(v))+0.06976*(0.14+0.7987*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*sin(v))+(-0.23288)*(12.15+0.8085*cos(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2))))+2.62314,(-0.06783)*(0.7105*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*cos(v))+0.99756*(0.14+0.7987*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*sin(v))+0.01628*(12.15+0.8085*cos(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2))))+(-0.18372),0.23345*(0.7105*sin(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2)))*cos(v))+0.97237*(12.15+0.8085*cos(u*(1.75-0.42*exp(-((v+1.3)/0.1)^2)-0.2*exp(-((v+1.15)/0.15)^2)-0.1*exp(-((v+2.12)/0.12)^2))))+0.31222,u,0,1,v,-pi,pi) | ref=hairCap color=#ac5232
((1+(-0.99888)*hk(t))*((hrx(t)-0.03)*sin(k*(1-0.64*(1-hdw(t)))))+(0.28283*hs(t)+0.03209*hk(t))*(0.14+(hry(t)-0.03)*cos(k*(1-0.64*(1-hdw(t)))))+((-0.95859)*hs(t)+0.00947*hk(t))*(hzz(t))-(-10.7981)*hs(t)-0.11083*hk(t),((-0.28283)*hs(t)+0.03209*hk(t))*((hrx(t)-0.03)*sin(k*(1-0.64*(1-hdw(t)))))+(1+(-0.08111)*hk(t))*(0.14+(hry(t)-0.03)*cos(k*(1-0.64*(1-hdw(t)))))+(0.03347*hs(t)+0.27111*hk(t))*(hzz(t))-0.37826*hs(t)-3.05384*hk(t),(0.95859*hs(t)+0.00947*hk(t))*((hrx(t)-0.03)*sin(k*(1-0.64*(1-hdw(t)))))+((-0.03347)*hs(t)+0.27111*hk(t))*(0.14+(hry(t)-0.03)*cos(k*(1-0.64*(1-hdw(t)))))+(1+(-0.92001)*hk(t))*(hzz(t))-(-0.00402)*hs(t)-(-10.36358)*hk(t),k,(-1.2),1.2,t,0.14318,0.7) | ref=hairUnder color=#ac5232
# Long locks. Down the back they fall straight in three layers (wide ones underneath, the main
# layer, thin lighter strands on top); at the sides they fan out over the shoulders and arms.
