//Braid
# A braided crown around the back of the head. The braid follows an oval ring on the dome: bdx, bdy, bdz
# give the direction from the head's centre to the ring at angle a, with ro scaling the ring (1 = its
# centre line). Its three strands weave as sin(tau) across the ring and sin(2 tau) in height, tau a third
# of a turn apart: the classic three-strand braid.
bdx(a,ro)=ro*2.24604*cos(a)
bdy(a,ro)=0.92718+ro*0.23408*sin(a)
bdz(a,ro)=0.37461-ro*0.57937*sin(a)
bdn(a,ro)=sqrt(bdx(a,ro)^2+bdy(a,ro)^2+bdz(a,ro)^2)
